\f1\fs22 On the VIP platform, Sarah\'92s hand drifted to her belly before she could stop it. Beside her, the Ermine Muller chair held very still. Hayley actually laughed. Kathy reached under her top and pulled the patch off her belly.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Sages sang the ditty a second then a third time.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Among the crowd, the kids leapt about like crazy Rumpelstiltskins. The Airborne tossed their air guitars and took up air ukuleles instead.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Sages pulled the music back. Kleo lifted his picking hand from the strings, the way a conductor asks a room to breathe with him, and set about the business of teaching half a million strangers a song they already half-knew. Before long, he had them singing on their own.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Louder!\'94 Chilo rasped.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The crowd sang teh whole round  louder.\
